{"v":1,"id":"01KYZ62F61EMERZ95HEFCSVETA","ts":"2026-08-01T17:31:11.425Z","initiative":"record-integrity","session":"7e987def-15b6-4689-97c7-1b7157f9289d","source":"claude-code","actor":"agent","user":"dev@jithin.io","type":"plan_updated","payload":{"plan":{"goal":"Stop cross-initiative event misroutes: pin hook writes to a session's home initiative, detect split sessions, and repair the live record.","phases":[{"name":"Phase 1 — Pin hook writes (stop the bleeding)","status":"active","tasks":[{"id":"1.1","status":"pending","title":"homeInitiative(session_id): resolve a session's home from the logs, bound-initiative-first with earliest session_started as tiebreak"},{"id":"1.2","status":"pending","title":"resolveBound consults the home pin before falling back to branch → bindings.json"},{"id":"1.3","status":"pending","title":"Tests: pinned routing survives a branch switch; new session still homes to branch; missing/corrupt data falls back"}]},{"name":"Phase 2 — Detect splits","status":"pending","tasks":[{"id":"2.1","status":"pending","title":"splitSessions detector: one session id registered or appearing in >1 initiative"},{"id":"2.2","status":"pending","title":"doctor reports splits as a problem (not a warning) with per-initiative event counts"}]},{"name":"Phase 3 — Repair the live record","status":"pending","tasks":[{"id":"3.1","status":"pending","title":"Reattribute the record-integrity/speed splits via correction events; leave merged initiatives as history"}]},{"name":"Phase 4 — Cross-session awareness (deferred from diagnosis)","status":"pending","tasks":[{"id":"4.1","status":"pending","title":"Derive git state (HEAD, ahead/behind, dirty) at render time — never log it"},{"id":"4.2","status":"pending","title":"UserPromptSubmit surfaces other sessions' movement since this session's last read"},{"id":"4.3","status":"pending","title":"Report all unwritten sessions, not just the newest (status.ts lastUnwrittenWithActivity)"}]}]}}}
{"v":1,"id":"01KYZ62R5GMRGX9YTV9SY8CGK7","ts":"2026-08-01T17:31:20.624Z","initiative":"record-integrity","session":"7e987def-15b6-4689-97c7-1b7157f9289d","source":"claude-code","actor":"agent","user":"dev@jithin.io","type":"decision_logged","payload":{"because":"The home is ALREADY in the truth log — session_started names it uniquely — so an index file would be duplicated state that can desync, needs pruning (99 sessions and counting), and forces a SPEC Record-layout change plus a gitignore decision (routing is a local runtime fact, but .sofar/ is committed wholesale). Deriving costs one file read on the common path (branch is correct → hit on the first log checked) and only pays the sibling scan in exactly the case where a misroute would otherwise have happened; total log volume is ~350KB. It is also self-healing: sessions registered before this fix get pinned correctly with no migration. Same philosophy as reading git state rather than logging it — a fact with an authoritative home is read, never copied.","chose":"Derive a session's home initiative from the event logs themselves — scan for the session's earliest session_started, checking the branch-bound initiative first and only falling through to siblings on a miss","over":"A new .sofar/sessions.json index mapping session_id to slug, written at registration and read by hooks"}}
