{"v":1,"id":"01KYZ6N49NGV6M1TF2YFPK4M0X","ts":"2026-08-01T17:41:22.869Z","initiative":"record-integrity","session":"7e987def-15b6-4689-97c7-1b7157f9289d","source":"claude-code","actor":"agent","user":"dev@jithin.io","type":"decision_logged","payload":{"because":"Measuring the 14 double-registrations in this repo inverted the hypothesis: 11 are hook-then-claude-code across two initiatives, i.e. the tear is NOT mostly a mid-session branch switch but lazy registration racing start_session — the hook registers in the branch's initiative, the binding moves, and start_session registers the SAME id again elsewhere. Hook pinning alone would have left those 11 intact. The source-based heuristic was rejected by the same data: the second registration is usually claude-code, so treating claude-code as deliberate would suppress 11 of 14 real splits.","chose":"Pin start_session to the session home as well as the hooks — branch resolution now applies only when `initiative` is explicit or the session has no home","over":"Pinning hooks alone (the original Phase 1 scope), or using envelope.source to tell a deliberate re-home from a misroute"}}
